  "assembly_notes": "Derive the swept envelope first: arm_span plus pivot_radius, head width/height plus tilt and roll radii, left/right wall_slide_travel inside the perimeter frame, and the selected VESA support footprint plus motion_clearance. The wall plate has no fixed center crossbar in the carriage sweep; a narrow vertical carriage captures the upper/lower perimeter rails, translates horizontally, and carries the arm's revolute wall pivot. Arm candidates preserve the sparse source families: open twin-cheek frame, tapered shroud, cast capsule, or compact rectangular link. The front arm terminates at a fixed candidate-specific height track; a separate Z-prismatic height carriage carries the complete screen head, with the fixed and moving halves of each counterweight, gas-spring, or rack mechanism assigned to the correct side of that joint. The three screen-motion candidates use distinct roll-hub, twin-sleeve/rod, and bored-swivel mechanisms; a compact carrier mounts the selected VESA plate directly, without a duplicate decorative stage plate. VESA candidates preserve separate wide twin-rail, bow-tie slotted-arm, butterfly, H-frame, crossed, independent-arm, and universal-plate load paths. The twin vertical rails are independent X-prismatic adjustment parts on the wide carrier. Every declared slot combination uses a locally sized shoulder/yoke/transition plate, never a compatibility gate. Revolute and continuous joints are AxisInterface/mate_axes joints registered with register_interface_mate. Height and depth tracks are kept outside the arm and head swept envelopes; palette and continuous dimensions are not diversity slots."
}
